calculated Credit, Bureau or other Financial Score&nbsp;</td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">Score&nbsp;</td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd">scr&nbsp;</td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd"><br></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Measurement</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Speed</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Speed</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Speed</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>sp</p></td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd"><br></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Label</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Telephone Number</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Telephone number, including fax, mobile, etc)</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Telno</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>tn</p></td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd"><br></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Label</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Text</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Free format text</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Txt</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>tx</p></td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd"><br></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Chronology</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Year</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Year</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Year</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>yr</p></td>
    <td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd"><br></td>
   </tr>
  </tbody>
 </table>
</div>
<div role=3D"region" aria-label=3D"Info" class=3D"confluence-information-ma=
cro  confluence-information-macro-information">
 <p class=3D"title conf-macro-render">DataHub - Landing</p><span role=3D"pr=
esentation" class=3D"aui-icon aui-icon-small aui-iconfont-info-filled confl=
uence-information-macro-icon"></span>
 <div class=3D"confluence-information-macro-body">
  <p>Data Sources that are Landed for loading to GuideWire DataHub&nbsp; (e=
.g. SAS Linux)&nbsp;should use the Physical Abbreviation where&nbsp;it alig=
ns with DataHub e.g. Code (CD) otherwise the Physical Class Word.</p>
 </div>
</div>
<p><br class=3D"atl-forced-newline">
  &nbsp;Examples of attributes:</p>
<ul>
 <li>Statement Cycle Seqno</li>
 <li>Product Desc</li>
 <li>Premium Rate</li>
 <li>Customer Last Debit Date</li>
 <li>Email Address Txt</li>
 <li>Bank Account Number Ref</li>
 <li>Policy Number Ref</li>
 <li>Person Forename Name or Person First Name</li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"LVDataNamingStandards-2.3.3LogicalRuleSet=E2=80=93AllLogicalObjec=
tNames">2.3.3 Logical Rule Set =E2=80=93 All Logical Object Names</h3>
<ul>
 <li>Maximum length is 50 characters.</li>
 <li>Component words separated by single spaces.</li>
 <li>Composed of unabbreviated words (where possible) and acronyms. Refer t=
o Appendix A for guidelines on creating abbreviations and acronyms.</li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"LVDataNamingStandards-2.3.4PhysicalRuleSet=E2=80=93AllPhysicalObj=
ects">2.3.4&nbsp;Physical Rule Set =E2=80=93 All Physical Objects</h3>
<p>This will vary based on the DBMS, for example, the recommended object st=
andard for Oracle would consists of uppercase characters and the use of imb=
edded underscores to delimit the constituent words, whereas for SQLServer, =
it is acceptable for the object names to be in mixed case with no underscor=
es. <br>
  Examples:-</p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
 <table class=3D"wrapped confluenceTable">
  <colgroup>
   <col>
   <col>
   <col>
   <col>
  </colgroup>
  <tbody>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p><em>Logical Name</em></p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p><em>Object Type</em></p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p><em>Physical Name =E2=80=93 Oracle</em></p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p><em>Physical Name =E2=80=93 SQLServer</em></p></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Customer First Name</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Column</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>CUSTOMER_FIRST_NAME</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>CustomerFirstName</p></td>
   </tr>
  </tbody>
 </table>
</div>
<p>Irrespective of DBMS the following generic standards will apply:-</p>
<ul>
 <li>length limit is maximum allowed by DBMS or does not exceed level of re=
asonableness (50 characters);</li>
 <li>consists of standard abbreviated words, where required, and acronyms;<=
/li>
 <li>may contain DBMS reserved words, provided that the whole name is not o=
ne;</li>
</ul>
<h4 id=3D"LVDataNamingStandards-2.3.4.1StepstoCreateaPhysicalName">2.3.4.1 =
Steps to Create a Physical Name</h4>
<p><br class=3D"atl-forced-newline">
  Step 1: The process starts with a long name. This can be an existing logi=
cal name (for physical names with corresponding logical names) or a newly c=
reated long name. If there is no corresponding logical name, follow the ste=
ps below to create a long name. Please note that the created long name will=
 not be registered in the Data Directory. <br class=3D"atl-forced-newline">
  If the physical object type has a corresponding logical object type, crea=
te a long name based on the rules for the logical object type. E.g. DOWNTIM=
E_LOG could be created as the long name a physical table that stores a log =
with the system downtime events, and with no corresponding logical entity. =
<br class=3D"atl-forced-newline">
  If the physical object type does not have a corresponding logical object =
type (a sequence, for example), create a long name that describes the purpo=
se of the object. E.g. POLICY_VERSION_DIALOGUE_VARIANCE_SEQNO. <br class=3D=
"atl-forced-newline">
  Step 2: Where name exceeds the DBMS limit or length exceeds that deemed r=
easonable, firstly replace component words, starting from the end of the co=
lumn name, with their corresponding abbreviated form where the word is long=
er than 8 characters in length (Refer to Appendix A for guidelines on creat=
ing abbreviations and acronyms), and replace spaces with underscores. <br c=
lass=3D"atl-forced-newline">
  Where the length still exceeds the DBMS limit then abbreviate words less =
than 8 characters using exceptional abbreviations (Refer to Appendix A). <b=
r class=3D"atl-forced-newline">
  Step 3: Compare the length of the abbreviated name against the length res=
triction of the target DBMS. If the name is too long, try the following:</p=
>
<ul>
 <li>Modify the long name to shorten it. Try synonyms, or remove component =
words. Make sure that the modified long name conforms to the naming rules.<=
/li>
 <li>Remove component words of least importance from the abbreviated name. =
Make sure you could reverse engineer the abbreviated name to a valid long n=
ame.</li>
 <li>Create an acronym that can replace several words in the long name.</li=
>
</ul>
<p><br class=3D"atl-forced-newline">
  Examples:- <br class=3D"atl-forced-newline">
  Personal Identification Number Assignment Method Code</p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
 <table class=3D"wrapped confluenceTable">
  <colgroup>
   <col>
   <col>
  </colgroup>
  <tbody>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Step 1</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Personal Identification Number Assignment Method Code</p></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Step 2</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>PRSNL_ID_NUMBER_ASGNT_METHOD_CODE (&gt; 30 character limit with abb=
reviations)</p></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Step 3</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>length('PIN_ASGNT_METHOD_CODE') =3D 21 chars (exceeds Oracle's 30 c=
haracter limit)</p></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Step 4</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Create an acronym for 'Personal Identification Number' and submit t=
o EIM for approval</p></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Result</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>PIN_ASGNT_METHOD_CODE</p></td>
   </tr>
  </tbody>
 </table>
</div>
<p><br class=3D"atl-forced-newline">
  Cash Transaction Fee File Key Activation Indicator</p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
 <table class=3D"wrapped confluenceTable">
  <colgroup>
   <col>
   <col>
  </colgroup>
  <tbody>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Step 1</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Cash Transaction Fee File Key Activation Indicator</p></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Step 2</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Cash_Trans_Fee_File_Key_Actvn_Ind</p></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Step 3</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>length('Cash_TrANS_Fee_File_Key_Actvn_Ind') =3D 33 (exceeds Oracle'=
s 30 character limit)</p></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Step 4</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Create an acronym for "Cash Transaction Fee" and submit to EIM for =
approval</p></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Result</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>CTF_FILE_KEY_ACTVN_IND</p></td>
   </tr>
  </tbody>
 </table>
</div>
<h2 id=3D"LVDataNamingStandards-2.4Conceptual/LogicalDataObjects">2.4 Conce=
ptual / Logical Data Objects</h2>
<h3 id=3D"LVDataNamingStandards-2.4.1DataModel(CDM,LDM)">2.4.1 Data Model (=
CDM, LDM)</h3>
<p>Represents information structures that capture business rules in order t=
o meet information system requirements. <br class=3D"atl-forced-newline">
  Guidelines:</p>
<ul>
 <li>Common Rule Set</li>
 <li>Logical Rule Set</li>
 <li>All characters in uppercase</li>
 <li>Name is singular or plural</li>
 <li>Noun phrase</li>
 <li>Does not contain class words</li>
</ul>
<p><br class=3D"atl-forced-newline">
  Examples:</p>
<ul>
 <li>M&amp;A ACCOUNT ANALYSIS</li>
 <li>ENTERPRISE DATA MODEL</li>
 <li>DATA WAREHOUSE SERVICES--DATA STAGING AREA</li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"LVDataNamingStandards-2.4.2SubjectArea">2.4.2 Subject Area</h3>
<p>A subset of objects taken from the whole pool of objects in a data model=
. <br class=3D"atl-forced-newline">
  Guidelines:</p>
<ul>
 <li>Common Rule Set</li>
 <li>Logical Rule Set</li>
 <li>All characters in uppercase</li>
 <li>Name can be singular or plural</li>
 <li>Noun phrase</li>
 <li>Does not contain class words</li>
</ul>
<p><br class=3D"atl-forced-newline">
  Examples:</p>
<ul>
 <li>APPLICATION PROCESSING</li>
 <li>CUSTOMERS</li>
 <li>ACCOUNTS</li>
 <li>PAYMENTS</li>
 <li>PRODUCTS</li>
 <li>SERVICES</li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"LVDataNamingStandards-2.4.3Entity">2.4.3 Entity</h3>
<p>Represents a business object or concept. <br class=3D"atl-forced-newline=
">
  Guidelines:</p>
<ul>
 <li>Common Rule Set</li>
 <li>Logical Rule Set</li>
 <li>All characters in uppercase</li>
 <li>Name is singular</li>
 <li>Noun phrase</li>
 <li>Does not contain class words</li>
 <li>Does not contain abbreviated words</li>
</ul>
<p><br class=3D"atl-forced-newline">
  Examples:</p>
<ul>
 <li>CUSTOMER</li>
 <li>ACCOUNT</li>
 <li>TRANSACTION</li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"LVDataNamingStandards-2.4.4LogicalView">2.4.4 Logical View</h3>
<p>Represents a business object or concept. Based on one or more entities. =
<br class=3D"atl-forced-newline">
  Guidelines:</p>
<ul>
 <li>Common Rule Set</li>
 <li>Logical Rule Set</li>
 <li>All characters in uppercase</li>
 <li>Name is singular</li>
 <li>Noun phrase</li>
 <li>Does not contain class words</li>
</ul>
<p><br class=3D"atl-forced-newline">
  Examples:</p>
<ul>
 <li>ACTIVE CUSTOMER</li>
 <li>CLOSED ACCOUNT</li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"LVDataNamingStandards-2.4.5Attribute">2.4.5 Attribute</h3>
<p>An English-like, singular name that is representative of the business me=
aning. <br class=3D"atl-forced-newline">
  Guidelines:</p>
<ul>
 <li>Common Rule Set</li>
 <li>Logical Rule Set</li>
 <li>First character of each word in uppercase, followed by lowercase chara=
cters =E2=80=93 except for acronyms</li>
 <li>Name is singular</li>
 <li>Noun phrase</li>
 <li>Selecting an attribute name can be difficult without first defining it=
. Developing a definition will help clarify the concept behind it and assis=
t in selecting the appropriate name.</li>
 <li>Unique within Data Directory.</li>
 <li>Consists of three parts in the following order: prime word, qualifier(=
s) and class word.</li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"LVDataNamingStandards-2.4.6Relationship">2.4.6 Relationship</h3>
<p>A relationship defines the association between entities and implements a=
 foreign key from the parent entity, where it is the primary key, to the ch=
ild entity. <br class=3D"atl-forced-newline">
  Guidelines:</p>
<ul>
 <li>Common Rule Set</li>
 <li>Logical Rule Set</li>
 <li>Defined in lowercase characters, except for acronyms</li>
 <li>Formed with an active verb or phrase in one direction and/or a passive=
 verb or phrase in the other direction; it captures a business rule</li>
 <li>Utilizes a present tense verb, unless there is a business reason for u=
sing past or future tense</li>
 <li>Does not contain <em>does</em>, <em>associates with</em>, <em>is relat=
ed to</em>, or <em>concerns--</em>names which do not convey any real inform=
ation</li>
</ul>
<p><br class=3D"atl-forced-newline">
  Examples:</p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
 <table class=3D"wrapped confluenceTable">
  <tbody>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Active</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Passive</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Active</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Passive</p></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>contains</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>is contained in</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>owns</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>is owned by</p></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>controls</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>is controlled by</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>regulates</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>is regulated by</p></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>describes</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>is described by</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>sells</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>is sold by</p></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>drives</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>is driven by</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>sponsors</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>is sponsored by</p></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>employs</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>is employed by</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>transports</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>is transported by</p></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>governs</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>is governed by</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>uses</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>is used by</p></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>married</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>is married to</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>manages</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>is managed by</p></td>
   </tr>
  </tbody>
 </table>
</div>
<h1 id=3D"LVDataNamingStandards-3PhysicalDataModelNamingStandards">3 Physic=
al Data Model Naming Standards</h1>
<h2 id=3D"LVDataNamingStandards-3.1Table">3.1 Table</h2>
<p>Usually, but not necessarily, the physical representation of a logical e=
ntity. <br class=3D"atl-forced-newline">
  General Guidelines:</p>
<ul>
 <li>Common Rule Set</li>
 <li>Physical Rule Set</li>
 <li>Is the standard name of the corresponding entity in the logical model.=
 The physical table name can be abbreviated if the maximum length of the ta=
ble name exceeds the length restrictions of the specific DBMS this needs to=
 take into account any index / constraint names so that they can be named i=
dentical to the table name, e.g. Oracle allows a maximum of 30 characters p=
er object. The name for a unique constraint could exceed the allowed length=
 if the table were named POLICY_VERSION_CREATION_EVENT as a minimum 4 chara=
cter suffix is required for a constraint, e.g. _UK1. Therefore, the table n=
ame should be abbreviated if it reaches the maximum allowed by the DBMS min=
us 5 characters (In this case, 25 characters), e.g. POLICY_VERSION_CRTN_EVE=
NT (table name) POLICY_VERSION_CRTN_EVENT_UK1 (constraint name).</li>
 <li>A prefix, although not mandatory, should be used for the following tab=
le types:-</li>
</ul>
<p><br></p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
 <table class=3D"wrapped confluenceTable">
  <colgroup>
   <col>
   <col>
   <col>
  </colgroup>
  <tbody>
   <tr>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">
     <p><strong>Table Type</strong></p></th>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">
     <p><strong>Definition</strong></p></th>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">
     <p><strong>Prefix</strong></p></th>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Landing Table</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Transient source system data table for loading into Staging Table. =
Weakly data typed, e.g. Varchar2(4000) to store any inbound string. Structu=
re mirrors source.</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>LND_</p></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>External Table</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Database view of an external file.</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>EXT_</p></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Working Table</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Temporary table</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>WRK_</p></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Reference Table</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Reference data / codified lookup data</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>R_</p></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Staging Table</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Persistent source system data table for non Data Vault schemas. Wea=
kly data typed to store any inbound string. Structure mirrors source.</p></=
td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>STG_</p></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Conformed Table</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Transient conformed view of data across source systems once data qu=
ality checks and business rules have been applied.</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>C_</p></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Bridge Table</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Table to manage many to many relationships within the Star Schema.<=
/p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>B_</p></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Materialised View</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Physicalised database view.</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>MV_</p></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Fact Table</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Fact table within a Star Schema. Typically aligned to a business pr=
ocess and contains the associated metrics.</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>F_</p></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Dimension Table</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Dimension table within a Star Schema. Typically reference data tabl=
es that give context to the Fact table.</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>D_</p></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Hub Table</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Table within the Data Vault schema storing business keys.</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>_HUB suffix</p>
     <p>(H_ legacy CRS/CQS)</p></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Satellite Table</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Table within the Data Vault schema =E2=80=93 a descriptive table re=
lating to Hub and Link tables.</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>_BSAT table suffix</p>
     <p>_SAT view suffix</p>
     <p>(S_ legacy CRS/CQS)</p></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Link Table</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Table within the Data Vault schema to link Hub and other Link table=
s</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>_LNK suffix</p>
     <p>(L_ legacy CRS/CQS)</p></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Hierarchy Link Table</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Data Vault Hierarchy Link Table</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>HL_</p></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Same as Link Table</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Data Vault Same as Link Table</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>SL_</p></td>
   </tr>
  </tbody>
 </table>
</div>
<h2 id=3D"LVDataNamingStandards-3.2PhysicalView">3.2 Physical View</h2>
<p>Usually, but not necessarily, the physical representation of a logical v=
iew. <br class=3D"atl-forced-newline">
  Guidelines:</p>
<ul>
 <li>Common Rule Set</li>
 <li>Physical Rule Set</li>
 <li>Is the standard abbreviated name of the corresponding view in the logi=
cal model, if there is one but with a prefix of 'V_'</li>
</ul>
<p>Example:</p>
<ul>
 <li>V_ACTV_CUST_BAL</li>
 <li>V_DWNTM_LOG</li>
</ul>
<h2 id=3D"LVDataNamingStandards-3.3Column">3.3 Column</h2>
<p>Usually, but not necessarily, the physical representation of an entity a=
ttribute. <br class=3D"atl-forced-newline">
  Guidelines:</p>
<ul>
 <li>Common Rule Set</li>
 <li>Physical Rule Set</li>
 <li>Is the standard abbreviated name of the corresponding entity attribute=
 in the logical model. Abbreviations should be taken from the standard abbr=
eviations list (see Appendix A).</li>
 <li>Always contains a class word at the end of the name</li>
</ul>
<p><br class=3D"atl-forced-newline">
  Examples:</p>
<ul>
 <li>CREDIT_HIRE_SLMNT_PACK_DATE (CREDIT HIRE SETTLEMENT PACK DATE is the c=
orresponding logical entity attribute)</li>
 <li>ERROR_NUMBER_CODE (no corresponding attribute)</li>
</ul>
<h2 id=3D"LVDataNamingStandards-3.4PrimaryKeyConstraint">3.4 Primary Key Co=
nstraint</h2>
<p>Usually, but not necessarily, the physical representation of a Primary K=
ey in the logical model. <br class=3D"atl-forced-newline">
  Guidelines:</p>
<ul>
 <li>Common Rule Set</li>
 <li>Physical Rule Set</li>
 <li>Named after the table by adding the suffix '_PK'</li>
</ul>
<p><br class=3D"atl-forced-newline">
  Examples:</p>
<ul>
 <li>CUSTOMER_PK</li>
 <li>POLICY_PK</li>
</ul>
<h2 id=3D"LVDataNamingStandards-3.5PrimaryIndex">3.5 Primary Index</h2>
<p>A Primary Index may be created automatically when a Primary Key constrai=
nt is defined. In this case, the index inherits the constraint name and can=
not be renamed. <br class=3D"atl-forced-newline">
  Guidelines:</p>
<ul>
 <li>Common Rule Set</li>
 <li>Physical Rule Set</li>
 <li>Same name as the Primary Key Constraint (named after the table by addi=
ng the suffix '_PK')</li>
</ul>
<p><br class=3D"atl-forced-newline">
  Example:</p>
<ul>
 <li>CUSTOMER_ACCOUNT_PK (generated automatically after the Primary Key con=
straint)</li>
</ul>
<h2 id=3D"LVDataNamingStandards-3.6ForeignKeyConstraint">3.6 Foreign Key Co=
nstraint</h2>
<p>Usually, but not necessarily, the physical representation of a Foreign K=
ey in the logical model. <br class=3D"atl-forced-newline">
  Guidelines:</p>
<ul>
 <li>Common Rule Set</li>
 <li>Physical Rule Set</li>
 <li>Named after the parent table by adding '_FKx'</li>
 <li>'x' is an optional sequence number that makes the index name unique ac=
ross multiple child tables that may reference the same parent table in the =
same database.</li>
</ul>
<p><br class=3D"atl-forced-newline">
  Examples:</p>
<ul>
 <li>PRODUCT_FK (constraint on ORDER.PRODUCT_ID referencing PRODUCT.PRODUCT=
_ID)</li>
 <li>ADDRESS_FK1 (constraint on ORDER.BILLING_ADDRESS_ID referencing ADDRES=
S.ADDRESS_ID)</li>
 <li>ADDRESS_FK2 (constraint on ORDER.SHIPPING_ADDRESS_ID referencing ADDRE=
SS.ADDRESS_ID)</li>
</ul>
<h2 id=3D"LVDataNamingStandards-3.7JoinIndex">3.7 Join Index</h2>
<p>Join Indexes are created for performance purposes to implement a foreign=
 key relationship, and have no logical counterpart. <br class=3D"atl-forced=
-newline">
  Guidelines:</p>
<ul>
 <li>Common Rule Set</li>
 <li>Physical Rule Set</li>
 <li>Name ends with the suffix '_JIx'</li>
 <li>'x' is an optional sequence number that makes the index name unique ac=
ross multiple child tables that may reference the same parent table in the =
same database.</li>
</ul>
<p><br class=3D"atl-forced-newline">
  Examples:</p>
<ul>
 <li>ADDRESS_JI (joins CUSTOMER and ADDRESS)</li>
 <li>ADDRESS_JI1(join ORDER.BILLING_ADDRESS_ID referencing ADDRESS.ADDRESS_=
ID and ACCOUNT)</li>
 <li>ADDRESS_JI2(join ORDER.SHIPPING_ADDRESS_ID referencing ADDRESS.ADDRESS=
_ID and ACCOUNT)</li>
</ul>
<h2 id=3D"LVDataNamingStandards-3.8UniqueConstraint">3.8 Unique Constraint<=
/h2>
<p>Usually, but not necessarily, the physical representation of an Alternat=
e Key in the logical model. <br class=3D"atl-forced-newline">
  Guidelines:</p>
<ul>
 <li>Common Rule Set</li>
 <li>Physical Rule Set</li>
 <li>Named after the table by adding the suffix '_UKx'</li>
 <li>'x' is an optional sequence number used to avoid naming collision</li>
</ul>
<p><br class=3D"atl-forced-newline">
  Examples:</p>
<ul>
 <li>PRODUCT_UK</li>
 <li>CUSTOMER_UK1, CUSTOMER_UK2</li>
</ul>
<h2 id=3D"LVDataNamingStandards-3.9UniqueIndex">3.9 Unique Index</h2>
<p>A Unique Secondary Index may be created automatically when a unique cons=
traint is defined. In this case, the index inherits the constraint name and=
 cannot be renamed. <br class=3D"atl-forced-newline">
  Guidelines:</p>
<ul>
 <li>Common Rule Set</li>
 <li>Physical Rule Set</li>
 <li>Named after the table by adding the suffix '_UKx'</li>
 <li>'x' is an optional sequence number used to avoid naming collision</li>
</ul>
<p><br class=3D"atl-forced-newline">
  Examples:</p>
<ul>
 <li>ACTIVE_CUSTOMER_BALANCE_UKI</li>
 <li>CUSTOMER_ACCOUNT_UK1, CUSTOMER_ADDRESS_UK2</li>
</ul>
<h2 id=3D"LVDataNamingStandards-3.10Non-UniqueIndex">3.10 Non-Unique Index<=
/h2>
<p>Join Indexes are created for performance purposes, and have no logical c=
ounterpart. <br class=3D"atl-forced-newline">
  Guidelines:</p>
<ul>
 <li>Common Rule Set</li>
 <li>Physical Rule Set</li>
 <li>Named after the table by adding the suffix '_NUx'</li>
 <li>'x' is an optional sequence number used to avoid naming collision</li>
</ul>
<p><br class=3D"atl-forced-newline">
  Examples:</p>
<ul>
 <li>PRODUCT_AK</li>
 <li>CUSTOMER_AK1, ACCOUNT_AK2</li>
</ul>
<h2 id=3D"LVDataNamingStandards-3.11CheckConstraint">3.11 Check Constraint<=
/h2>
<p>Usually, but not necessarily, the physical representation of a Validatio=
n Rule in the logical model. <br class=3D"atl-forced-newline">
  Guidelines:</p>
<ul>
 <li>Common Rule Set</li>
 <li>Physical Rule Set</li>
 <li>Column level check constraints are named after the column name by addi=
ng the suffix '_CCx'</li>
 <li>Table level check constraints are named after the table by adding the =
suffix '_TCx'</li>
 <li>'x' is an optional sequence number that makes the check constraint nam=
e unique within the table</li>
</ul>
<p><br class=3D"atl-forced-newline">
  Examples:</p>
<ul>
 <li>CUSTOMER_NUMBER_REF_CC (column level check constraint)</li>
 <li>CUSTOMER_ADDRESS_TC1, CUSTOMER_ADDRESS_TC2 (table level check constrai=
nts)</li>
</ul>
<h1 id=3D"LVDataNamingStandards-AppendixAAbbreviationsandAcronyms">Appendix=
 A Abbreviations and Acronyms</h1>
<h2 id=3D"LVDataNamingStandards-GuidelinesfortheuseofStandardAbbreviationsa=
ndAcronyms">Guidelines for the use of Standard Abbreviations and Acronyms</=
h2>
<p>Abbreviations fall into four categories; standard abbreviations, excepti=
onal abbreviations, phrase abbreviations or acronym abbreviations, which ap=
ply to the naming standards in the following circumstances:-</p>
<h3 id=3D"LVDataNamingStandards-StandardAbbreviations">Standard Abbreviatio=
ns</h3>
<p>Where the length of the object name in the physical schema exceeds the D=
BMS limitation, prime/qualifier words exceeding 8 characters should be abbr=
eviated, starting from the right-hand side of the column name.</p>
<p>Exceptional Abbreviations</p>
<p>If after abbreviating all prime/qualifier words over 8 characters an obj=
ect name it is still too long, then an exceptional abbreviation can be used=
 to further reduce the length of the name where the words are less than 8 c=
haracters.</p>
<h3 id=3D"LVDataNamingStandards-PhraseAbbreviations">Phrase Abbreviations</=
h3>
<p>Common phrases used within the LV Business Areas or Systems can be used =
within prime/qualifier words or other objects, ie, Physical Table, only if =
the length of the object name exceeds the DBMS limitation.</p>
<h3 id=3D"LVDataNamingStandards-AcronymAbbreviations">Acronym Abbreviations=
</h3>
<p>Common acronyms used externally to LV or within the LV business areas ca=
n be used within column names. These can be used in any circumstance.</p>
<p>The Standard Abbreviations and Acronyms List within this document should=
 be consulted to check if there is already an abbreviation or an acronym fo=
r the word in question.</p>
<ul>
 <li>Abbreviations should be created based upon the singular form of the wo=
rd. For verbs, use the singular present tense.</li>
 <li>Duplicated letters do not appear in the abbreviated word. For example,=
 ASSESSMENT is abbreviated as ASMNT.</li>
 <li>Abbreviations should begin with the same letter of the fully spelled w=
ord. For example, the letter X should not replace the letters EX (as in <em=
>expire</em>) or CROSS (as in <em>cross-reference</em>).</li>
 <li>Avoid creating acronyms or abbreviations that result in an English wor=
d. For example, Number =3D NO.</li>
 <li>The created abbreviated word or acronym must be unique. E.g., an abbre=
viation and an acronym cannot share the same name.</li>
</ul>
<p><br class=3D"atl-forced-newline">
  Submit the proposed abbreviation to the EIM for approval and inclusion in=
 the Standard Abbreviation List.</p>
<h2 id=3D"LVDataNamingStandards-A1StandardAbbreviationsandAcronymsList">&nb=
sp;A1 Standard Abbreviations and Acronyms List</h2>
